  "description": "Governance patterns for orgs where Apex triggers and record-triggered Flows both run on the same object: field-write conflict prevention, single-entry-point consolidation, recursion guards across automation types, and automation inventory. Use when inheriting a mixed-automation org, adding a Flow to an object that already has triggers, or resolving silent field-overwrite bugs. NOT for save order of execution \u2014 use apex/order-of-execution-deep-dive. NOT for Flow-only patterns \u2014 use flow/record-triggered-flow-patterns.",
  "file_location": "skills/apex/trigger-and-flow-coexistence",
  "id": "apex/trigger-and-flow-coexistence",
  "inputs": [
    "Object name and list of all active automations (triggers, flows, workflow rules, process builder)",
    "Description of the field-write conflict or recursion symptom",
    "Whether the org has a single-trigger-per-object pattern or multiple triggers"
  ],
